🔹 When to Use Which?
✅ Use Dijkstra When:
You need the shortest path between nodes.
The graph may have cycles but no negative weights.
You need to find the fastest way in networks (road maps, internet routing, etc.).
✅ Use Topological Sorting When:
You need a valid ordering of tasks or dependencies.
The graph is a DAG (no cycles allowed).
Examples: Task scheduling, compilation order, course prerequisites.
